        "id": "item_4bdc1f7184c5400c",
        "kind": "paper",
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28327",
        "title": "How Diverse Are Layered Safeguards? Estimands and Measurement for Ensembles of LLM Jailbreak Defenses",
        "source": "arXiv",
        "summary": "Practitioners protect large language models (LLMs) by stacking safeguards: a likelihood filter, a guard classifier, hidden-state probes, a decoding-time intervention. Such a stack is an ensemble of learned detectors, and ensemble theory states when combination pays: when members fail on different inputs. Stacking is recommended throughout the LLM security literature, but this condition has not been measured for any pair of safeguards. The conditi",
